Z||000019||California Kid||11-18-2001||06:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gtjeff:<BR><B>California Kid, since you live in Detroit area have you considered parking your ride in front of GM's Renaisance Center and let some of the employees see what Pontiac Excitement really is?<BR>Nice vette killer.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>They know what it looks like! Had it on display at the GM Tech Center Show early this year, took 3rd Place for 1974 to 1994 Modified All Makes and Models. Car was only 3 days out of the paint shop, no fine detailing. Sure got a lot of attention there!<P>Hopefully now that Bob Lutz is a key factor at GM, maybe we'll see some styling changes that grab the eye. He was only on board there a few days and he cancelled 3/4's of the future model "Clays" they were working on.||||reg||1
Z||000020||WKDFIRO||11-20-2001||12:15 AM||||Hopefully now that we have a CAR guy and not another bean counter at GM maybe we can see some real cars coming out again. They have a lot to make up for with the Aztec. Its a long shot but the mid-90s Impala SS started off as a custom show car that made its way to the top brass...history repeat itself? Yeah right.<P>Thanks for the trip down memory lane! It reminded me when I got to turn the wheels in the large parking lot at the Anaheim Stadium. I was so impressed at how easy it was to control throttle wise. What a great V8. <P>Zumalt that is... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||6
